WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
A stone inscription from ancient
Moab, carved around 840 BCE.

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:10.230
On it, King Mesha boasts that he devoted
the people of an Israelite town to his

3
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.240
god.

4
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.920
The Bible uses the same idea,
herem, in Israel's own war stories,

5
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.740
starting with Jericho.

6
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:21.400
Yet the same scriptures call
God merciful and gracious,

7
00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.030
slow to anger.

8
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.790
So how have readers made sense of both?

9
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.910
In this mission, you'll read the law of
herem and follow it through Joshua and

10
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.460
the story of Saul.

11
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:36.540
Then you'll weigh up a hard question:
can a warrior God and a compassionate God

12
00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.200
be reconciled?

13
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:43.000
Your mission: find out how readers have
made sense of mercy and destruction in

14
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.360
the same scriptures.
